{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Defined-name calculation shared by every engine (py_toolkit, py_canonical, rust toolkit, rust canonical). Expected values are independent arithmetic over the listed cells; messages are Workbook Forge's own typed refusals. Each case is one formula cell on its sheet, in its own column of row 10 in case order. A diagnostic case names the toolkit code; the canonical model maps name_cycle to cycle/cycle, resource_limit to resource_limit, parse_error to parse_error unsupported_formula to unsupported_formula/unsupported and invalid_reference to invalid_reference/invalid_reference. XFE1 is cell-shaped past the grid and stays an invalid reference, even when a name of that spelling exists. A case without a message checks the code only (parse messages are engine-specific). See docs/defined-names.md.",
  "sheets": [
    "Inputs",
    "Calc",
    "Other"
  ],
  "cells": {
    "Inputs!A1": 0.5,
    "Inputs!A2": 1000,
    "Inputs!B1": 10,
    "Inputs!B2": 20,
    "Inputs!B3": 30,
    "Calc!A1": 5
  },
  "names": [
    {
      "name": "Rate",
      "sheet": null,
      "formula": "Inputs!$A$1",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
